# Module documentation (backend + frontend)

When you **create or meaningfully change** a first-party module under `backend/Modules/*` or `frontend/src/modules/*`:

## Required artifacts

1. **`README.md`** in the module root (BE and FE separately if both exist)
   - Purpose, quick path map, permissions/gates, runtime deps (if any)
   - Links to `docs/sis/*.md`, `docs/extensions/*.md`, or architecture docs when relevant
   - Short “Agent notes” (do/don’t for the next agent)
2. **`CHANGELOG.md`** in the same module root
   - [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.1.0/) style
   - Put new entries under `[Unreleased]` with `### Added` / `### Changed` / `### Fixed` (as needed)
   - Move to a dated/versioned section when the pack ships a versioned release

## Dual-layer changelog (wajib pahami)

| Layer | Path | Isi |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **School SIS Domain** | `backend/Modules/School/CHANGELOG.md`, `frontend/src/modules/School/CHANGELOG.md` | Detail domain Akademik, Kesiswaan, GTK, Sarpras, Persuratan, PPDB, OSIS |
| **Core domains** | `Modules/Core/{System,Infra,Security}/CHANGELOG.md` (+ FE) | Wajib per domain kernel; `Core/CHANGELOG.md` = index |
| **Other Modules** | `backend/Modules/*/CHANGELOG.md`, `frontend/src/modules/*/CHANGELOG.md` | Layout, Publishing, Member, Mail, Forms, Analytics, dll. |
| **Theme package** | `frontend/src/modules/Layout/views/themes/<slug>/CHANGELOG.md` | Perubahan khusus tema publik (mis. `sarangenge`) |
| **Root** | `/CHANGELOG.md` | Ringkas release-facing + pointer (bukan duplikat esai) |

How-to: [`docs/guides/update-changelog.md`](../../docs/guides/update-changelog.md).  
Versioning (produk + per pack): [`docs/guides/release-and-versioning.md`](../../docs/guides/release-and-versioning.md) · `npm run modules:versions:check`.  
Template: [`docs/templates/changelog-module.md`](../../docs/templates/changelog-module.md).

## Also update

- Domain doc if one exists (e.g. `docs/sis/*.md` for School, `docs/extensions/ja-mail.md` for Mail)
- Pack **`manifest.json` `version`** (or theme `theme.json`) when changing runtime code — forward-only SemVer; locales count as PATCH
- Root `CHANGELOG.md` `[Unreleased]` with a one-line pointer for user-visible **or** system-docs changes
- Task brief § Hasil when scale M+ (`docs/work/`)

## Do not

- Leave hanging “future backlog” items that belong to other systems (e.g. KataMPI CBT engine or MTA/IMAP)
- Skip changelog when behavior, API, permissions, or public theme UX change
- Put client/tenant-specific hardcoded data into changelogs or seeders
